1. Qt 6.10.2 — LGPL-3.0-only (open-source build)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Component        Qt 6.10.2, open-source build (`C:\Qt\licenseInfo.txt`: "License type
                 [Opensource]"). Version confirmed by `qmake -query QT_VERSION`.
Modules linked   Qt6Core, Qt6Gui, Qt6Widgets, Qt6Svg, Qt6Multimedia, Qt6MultimediaWidgets,
                 Qt6Concurrent, Qt6Network. Qt6Test is linked only by the `test_*` targets and is
                 NOT part of the shipped application.
How it ships     Dynamically linked DLLs, deployed by `windeployqt`
                 (`cmake/SpellVisionQtDeploy.cmake`). windeployqt also copies Qt's own bundled
                 third-party components (image and multimedia plugins and their dependencies);
                 Qt's manifest for those is
                 `C:\Qt\Docs\Qt-6.10.2\qtdoc\licenses-used-in-qt.html`.
Licence          LGPL-3.0-only for the modules above. Some Qt tools and add-on components are
                 GPL-3.0-only; none of those is redistributed by SpellVision.
Licence text     `C:\Qt\Licenses\LICENSE`      — GPL-3.0 and LGPL-3.0 full texts
                 `C:\Qt\Licenses\COPYING.txt`  — Apache-2.0 (used by parts of Qt)
                 `C:\Qt\Licenses\LICENSE.FDL`  — GFDL-1.3 (documentation)
                 `C:\Qt\Licenses\Copyright.txt`— third parties bundled with the Qt installer
                 The installer MUST copy these next to the application.

⚠ OBLIGATION — RELINKING. The LGPL-3.0 conveys Qt on the condition that a recipient can replace the
Qt libraries with a modified version and relink the application against them. SpellVision satisfies
this by dynamic linking only: the Qt DLLs sit beside `SpellVision.exe` and a recipient may replace
them in place. Three things therefore must not change without re-examining this obligation:

  1. Qt must not be statically linked into `SpellVision.exe`.
  2. The Qt DLLs must remain replaceable — not signed-and-verified by the app, not packed into a
     single-file bundle that the user cannot open, not renamed such that a stock Qt build cannot
     substitute.
  3. The shipped product must carry this notice, the LGPL-3.0 text, and a statement of the Qt
     version so a recipient can obtain the corresponding source
     (https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/6.10/6.10.2/single/).

If Qt is ever modified, the modified source must also be offered.


